{"id":"ltc-related-payments-ca","title":"Nursing homes paying a quarter or more of their costs to related companies","question":"Across California, which nursing homes send the largest share of their spending to companies under common ownership, and where do San Francisco homes stand?","finding":"In 2025, 935 of 1070 California nursing homes with at least $2 million of expenses listed transactions with related parties; the middle one sent 7.6% of its expenses to them. 15 homes sent 25% or more (4 in the Bay Area). California homes listed $1,496.6 million of related-party transactions in 2025, against $1,173.1 million in 2019. The highest San Francisco share is The Sequoias San Francisco at 29.0%.","how":"Report year 2025 (as submitted). Share = the sum of positive transaction amounts on page 10.4, lines 30 to 99, divided by total health-care expenses on page 8, line 200. Skilled-nursing licences only; homes with less than $2 million of expenses are left out. Rent and management columns are read from the cost centre and description each home gave.","limits":"A home that leases its building from its owner's property company will show its whole rent here, and a home whose staff are employed by an affiliate will show its whole payroll: neither is a sign of overcharging. Medi-Cal limits what may be claimed for these purchases to the related company's cost, so the share of costs passed on to Medi-Cal can be lower than the share paid. The question the screen raises is price: whether the rent or fee was above what an unrelated party would charge, which the file does not show.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"home","t":"Nursing home","type":"org"},{"k":"city","t":"City","type":"text"},{"k":"county","t":"County","type":"text"},{"k":"control","t":"Type","type":"text"},{"k":"paidRelated","t":"Paid to related parties","type":"usd"},{"k":"expenses","t":"Total expenses","type":"usd"},{"k":"share","t":"Share of expenses","type":"pct"},{"k":"rent","t":"Of which rent and leases","t